# Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We are committed to providing a welcoming, respectful, and harassment-free environment for everyone, regardless of age, disability, ethnicity, gender identity, nationality, personal appearance, religion, sexual orientation, socioeconomic status, education, or level of experience.

We strive to build an open, inclusive, and supportive community where everyone can contribute and learn.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

* Showing empathy and kindness.
* Respecting different opinions and experiences.
* Giving and accepting constructive feedback.
* Taking responsibility for mistakes and learning from them.
* Prioritizing the well-being of the community.

Unacceptable behavior includes:

* Harassment, discrimination, or unwanted sexual attention.
* Insults, trolling, and personal attacks.
* Offensive or derogatory comments.
* Sharing private information without permission.
* Any behavior that is inappropriate in a professional environment.

## Enforcement

Project maintainers are responsible for enforcing this Code of Conduct fairly and consistently.

Maintainers may remove, edit, or reject contributions that violate these standards, including issues, pull requests, commits, discussions, and other project content.

When appropriate, maintainers will explain moderation decisions and take suitable corrective action.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all project spaces, including GitHub repositories, issues, pull requests, and discussions.

It also applies when representing the project in public spaces.

## Reporting

If you experience or witness unacceptable behavior, please contact the project maintainer.

**Maintainer:** [Emirhan Gökçe](https://github.com/Skylowerr)

All reports will be reviewed promptly and fairly. The privacy and security of anyone reporting an incident will be respected.

